      "content": "Absolutely! Claude Code is my sibling and handles this kind of multi-file project beautifully. Here's a handoff optimized for it. 🚀\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n## 🛠️ Terminal setup\n\n\n\n```bash\n\nmkdir gemach-connect && cd gemach-connect\n\nclaude\n\n```\n\n\n\nOnce Claude Code launches, paste the entire prompt below:\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n## 📋 PROMPT TO PASTE INTO CLAUDE CODE\n\n\n\n```\n\nI want you to build a complete, production-ready full-stack web application in this empty directory. Please plan the structure first, then create every file end-to-end. Do not leave placeholders, TODOs, or partial implementations. When you're done, run the setup commands yourself and verify the build succeeds.\n\n\n\n# PROJECT: Gemach Connect\n\n\n\nA directory platform for Jewish community members to find and list Gemachs (free lending organizations) across North America. Users can browse, search, register, list their own Gemachs, and message each other to arrange donations and pickups.\n\n\n\n# TECH STACK\n\n- Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript\n\n- Prisma ORM + SQLite (file:./dev.db)\n\n- NextAuth v4 (Credentials provider, JWT strategy)\n\n- Tailwind CSS\n\n- bcryptjs, zod, lucide-react, sonner, date-fns, clsx, tailwind-merge\n\n\n\n# WORKFLOW\n\n1. Create package.json and install dependencies (`npm install`)\n\n2. Create all config files (next, tailwind, postcss, tsconfig, .env, .gitignore)\n\n3. Create Prisma schema and run `npx prisma db push`\n\n4. Create seed script and run `npm run seed`\n\n5. Create lib files (prisma, auth, utils, types)\n\n6. Create all API routes\n\n7. Create global CSS and root layout\n\n8. Create shared components\n\n9. Create all pages\n\n10. Run `npm run build` to verify no errors\n\n11. Report success with login credentials\n\n\n\n# DATA MODEL (prisma/schema.prisma)\n\nSQLite datasource, url = \"file:./dev.db\"\n\n\n\n**User**: id (cuid), email (unique), name, password, phone? (optional), createdAt, relations: gemachs, sentMsgs, receivedMsgs\n\n\n\n**Gemach**: id, name, category, description, address, city, state, country (default \"USA\"), zipCode, phone, email?, hours, website?, imageUrl?, latitude? (Float), longitude? (Float), createdAt, updatedAt, ownerId → User onDelete Cascade, messages\n\n\n\n**Message**: id, content, type (default \"inquiry\"), read (default false), createdAt, gemachId → Gemach Cascade, senderId → User relation \"sender\" Cascade, receiverId → User relation \"receiver\" Cascade\n\n\n\n# SEED DATA (prisma/seed.ts)\n\n- Clear existing data\n\n- Create demo user: email `demo@gemach.app`, password `demo1234` (bcrypt hashed, 10 rounds), name \"Demo User\", phone\n\n- Create 8 additional owner users (owner1@gemach.app etc.) with same hashed password\n\n- Create 12 realistic gemachs across: Brooklyn NY, Lakewood NJ, Monsey NY, Passaic NJ, Baltimore MD, Los Angeles CA, Chicago IL, Toronto ON (country \"Canada\"), Miami Beach FL, Cleveland OH, Monroe NY, Brooklyn NY\n\n- Categories to cover: Baby Items, Wedding Gowns, Medical Equipment, Kitchen Supplies, Clothing, Books & Seforim, Furniture, Toys, Simcha Supplies, Food\n\n- Realistic names like \"Chesed Baby Gemach\", \"Kallah Kollel Gowns\", \"Bikur Cholim Medical Equipment\", \"Tomchei Shabbos\", \"Yad Ezra Clothing\", \"Ohr HaTorah Seforim\"\n\n- Hours: \"Sun-Thu 9am-9pm, Fri 9am-2pm\"\n\n- First gemach owned by demo user, rest distributed\n\n- Create 5 sample messages of mixed types (inquiry, donation, pickup) between users\n\n\n\n# AUTHENTICATION (src/lib/auth.ts)\n\nNextAuth options with CredentialsProvider. Validate email/password via bcrypt.compare against DB. JWT strategy. Custom signIn page at \"/login\". Callbacks: jwt stores user.id in token; session exposes id on session.user. Secret from process.env.NEXTAUTH_SECRET with dev fallback.\n\n\n\nAlso create src/types/next-auth.d.ts extending Session so user has id, email, name.\n\n\n\n# API ROUTES (src/app/api/)\n\n\n\n**auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts**: standard NextAuth handler, export GET and POST\n\n\n\n**register/route.ts** (POST): zod schema (name min 2, email valid, password min 6, phone optional). Check email uniqueness (return 400 if exists). Bcrypt hash. Create user. Return user without password.\n\n\n\n**gemachs/route.ts**:\n\n- GET: query params `q` (search name/description/city using contains), `category`, `state`, `mine=true` (filter by session user id). Include owner {name, email}. Order by createdAt desc.\n\n- POST: require session (401 if none). Create gemach with ownerId from session.\n\n\n\n**gemachs/[id]/route.ts**:\n\n- GET: include owner {id, name, email, phone}\n\n- PUT: require session, verify ownership (403 if not owner), update\n\n- DELETE: require session, verify ownership, delete\n\n\n\n**messages/route.ts**:\n\n- GET: require session. Return messages where user is sender OR receiver. Include sender {name, email}, receiver {name, email}, gemach {id, name}. Order createdAt desc.\n\n- POST: require session. Body {gemachId, content, type}. Look up gemach to get owner. Create message with senderId=session.user.id, receiverId=gemach.ownerId. Return with includes.\n\n\n\n**messages/[id]/route.ts** (PATCH): Mark message as read.\n\n\n\n# GLOBAL STYLES (src/app/globals.css)\n\nTailwind directives + these component classes:\n\n- body: bg-gray-50, text-gray-900, system font stack\n\n- .btn: inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 font-medium transition\n\n- .btn-primary: bg-primary-600 text-white hover:bg-primary-700\n\n- .btn-secondary: bg-white border border-gray-300 text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50\n\n- .btn-danger: bg-red-600 text-white hover:bg-red-700\n\n- .input: w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-3 py-2 focus:border-primary-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary-500/20\n\n- .card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200\n\n- .label: block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1\n\n\n\nTailwind config: extend colors.primary scale — 50:#eff6ff, 500:#3b82f6, 600:#2563eb, 700:#1d4ed8\n\n\n\n# LAYOUT & PROVIDERS\n\n- src/app/layout.tsx: HTML shell, Providers wrapper, Sonner Toaster (position=\"top-right\" richColors), title \"Gemach Connect\"\n\n- src/components/Providers.tsx ('use client'): wrap children in SessionProvider\n\n\n\n# COMPONENTS (src/components/)\n\n\n\n**Sidebar.tsx** ('use client'): 256px wide, sticky, full height. Logo: Heart icon in primary-600 rounded square + \"Gemach Connect\" text. Nav items with lucide icons:\n\n- Dashboard → /dashboard (Home)\n\n- Browse Gemachs → /gemachs (Search)\n\n- My Gemachs → /dashboard/my-gemachs (Heart)\n\n- Add Gemach → /dashboard/new (Plus)\n\n- Messages → /dashboard/messages (MessageSquare)\n\n- Profile → /dashboard/profile (User)\n\n\n\nActive link: bg-primary-50 text-primary-700. Bottom: user name/email from useSession + Sign Out button (signOut with callbackUrl:'/').\n\n\n\n**GemachCard.tsx**: Link to /gemachs/{id}, card with hover:shadow-md. Shows: name (semibold), category badge (primary-50 bg, primary-700 text), description (line-clamp-2), then icon rows for MapPin+city/state, Clock+hours (truncate), Phone+phone.\n\n\n\n**EmptyState.tsx**: Props {icon: LucideIcon, title, description, action?}. Centered layout: gray-100 circle with icon, title (font-semibold), description (text-gray-500), optional action button.\n\n\n\n**Spinner.tsx**: Exports `Spinner` (animate-spin border) and `PageLoader` (centered spinner in flex py-20).\n\n\n\n**GemachForm.tsx** ('use client'): Reusable for create/edit. Props {initial?, id?}. Fields: name, category dropdown (Baby Items, Wedding Gowns, Medical Equipment, Kitchen Supplies, Clothing, Books & Seforim, Furniture, Toys, Simcha Supplies, Food, Other), description (textarea), address, city, state dropdown (NY, NJ, CA, FL, IL, MD, PA, OH, MI, MA, TX, ON, QC), zipCode, phone, email (optional), hours (default \"Sun-Thu 9am-9pm, Fri 9am-2pm\"), website (optional). Submit: POST /api/gemachs or PUT /api/gemachs/{id}. Loading state on button. Toast success/error. router.push('/dashboard/my-gemachs') on success.\n\n\n\n# PAGES\n\n\n\n**src/app/page.tsx** (public landing): Header with logo + Log In / Sign Up buttons. Hero: \"Find Gemachs Across North America\" + subtitle + CTAs (Browse Gemachs → /gemachs, List Your Gemach → /register). 3 feature cards using Search, MessageSquare, MapPin icons. Footer with demo credentials line.\n\n\n\n**src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx** ('use client'): Centered card, Heart logo. Prefilled demo@gemach.app / demo1234. signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect:false}). Toast + redirect /dashboard. Link to /register.\n\n\n\n**src/app/(auth)/register/page.tsx** ('use client'): Form (name, email, phone optional, password min 6). POST /api/register → auto signIn → toast → redirect /dashboard.\n\n\n\n**src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx** (server): getServerSession → redirect /login if none. Render Sidebar + main content.\n\n\n\n**src/app/dashboard/page.tsx** ('use client'): Parallel fetch: my gemachs, messages, all gemachs. Show 3 stat cards (icon in colored square, count, label). Quick Actions section with 3 buttons (Add Gemach, Browse, Messages).\n\n\n\n**src/app/dashboard/my-gemachs/page.tsx** ('use client'): Fetch /api/gemachs?mine=true. List with Edit link and Delete button. Optimistic delete: update state first, rollback on error. Empty state with \"Add Gemach\" CTA.\n\n\n\n**src/app/dashboard/new/page.tsx**: Render <GemachForm />.\n\n\n\n**src/app/dashboard/edit/[id]/page.tsx** ('use client'): Fetch gemach, render <GemachForm initial={gemach} id={id} />.\n\n\n\n**src/app/dashboard/messages/page.tsx** ('use client'): Fetch /api/messages. Each message: color-coded type badge (inquiry=blue, donation=green, pickup=amber), sent/received label, gemach name link, sender/receiver name, relative time via date-fns formatDistanceToNow, content. Empty state.\n\n\n\n**src/app/dashboard/profile/page.tsx** ('use client'): Session user in card with User icon avatar.\n\n\n\n**src/app/gemachs/layout.tsx**: Same auth-protected layout as dashboard.\n\n\n\n**src/app/gemachs/page.tsx** ('use client'): Search input (Search icon inside, debounced 300ms) + category dropdown. Refetch on change. Grid of GemachCards (1/2/3 cols responsive). PageLoader + EmptyState handled.\n\n\n\n**src/app/gemachs/[id]/page.tsx** ('use client'): Full details in card with icon rows (MapPin, Clock, Phone, Mail, User). Back button. If session user is owner → Edit link. If not owner → \"Contact this Gemach\" button reveals message form (type selector: General Inquiry / I want to Donate / Pickup Request + textarea). POST /api/messages. Toast success.\n\n\n\n# CONFIG DETAILS\n\n- .env: NEXTAUTH_SECRET=\"dev-secret-change-me-in-production-min-32-chars\" and NEXTAUTH_URL=\"http://localhost:3000\"\n\n- .gitignore: node_modules, .next, .env, prisma/dev.db*, .DS_Store\n\n- next.config.js: `module.exports = { reactStrictMode: true }`\n\n- postcss.config.js: standard tailwind + autoprefixer\n\n- tsconfig.json: Next.js standard with @/* → ./src/* path alias\n\n- package.json scripts: dev (next dev), build (prisma generate && prisma db push && next build), start, seed (tsx prisma/seed.ts), postinstall (prisma generate)\n\n\n\n# GLOBAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n- 'use client' on ALL files using hooks or browser APIs\n\n- Every form has loading state (disabled + text change) during submission\n\n- Every list has empty state with lucide icon + message + optional CTA\n\n- Toast notifications on all mutations via sonner\n\n- Optimistic UI on delete (update local state first, rollback on error)\n\n- Debounced search (300ms via setTimeout in useEffect)\n\n- Owner-only permissions enforced on BOTH server (API 403) AND UI (hide buttons)\n\n- Responsive: grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\n\n- Polished: rounded-xl cards, subtle shadows, blue primary accent\n\n- All buttons use .btn classes; all inputs use .input\n\n\n\n# FINAL VERIFICATION STEPS\n\nAfter creating all files, run these commands yourself:\n\n1. `npm install` (if not done)\n\n2. `npx prisma generate`\n\n3. `npx prisma db push`\n\n4. `npm run seed`\n\n5. `npm run build` — must succeed with no errors\n\n\n\nIf the build fails, read the errors and fix them until it succeeds. Then report:\n\n- ✅ Build succeeded\n\n- 📁 File count\n\n- 🔑 Login: demo@gemach.app / demo1234\n\n- 🚀 Run `npm run dev` and visit http://localhost:3000\n\n\n\nBegin now. Plan briefly, then execute.\n\n```\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n## 💡 Claude Code specific tips\n\n\n\n**Claude Code's superpowers vs Aider:**\n\n- ✅ It reads files back to check its own work\n\n- ✅ Runs commands and sees output\n\n- ✅ Fixes errors automatically when builds fail\n\n- ✅ Handles multi-file refactors without losing context\n\n\n\n**Handy commands during the session:**\n\n- `/clear` — reset context if it gets confused\n\n- `/undo` — undo last edit\n\n- Just type naturally — \"the build failed with X, fix it\" or \"add loading state to the messages page\"\n\n\n\n**If it asks for confirmation on commands**, say `yes` or run in `--dangerously-skip-permissions` mode (only in this clean dir):\n\n```bash\n\nclaude --dangerously-skip-permissions\n\n```\n\n\n\n**After it's done, if you want to deploy:**\n\nJust say to Claude Code:\n\n```\n\nNow help me deploy this to Vercel. Switch Prisma to Postgres (I'll use Neon), update the build script, and walk me through the deployment steps.\n\n```\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n## 🏁 Expected outcome\n\n\n\nClaude Code will:\n\n1. Plan the file structure\n\n2. Create everything (~40 files)\n\n3. Install deps\n\n4. Run migrations + seed\n\n5. Verify build passes\n\n6. Tell you: \"✅ Done! Run `npm run dev` and log in with demo@gemach.app / demo1234\"\n\n\n\nShould take ~3-5 minutes depending on your machine. \n\n\n\nCome back if anything breaks — happy to debug! 🎉    or this: tell me which one is better to build:  ## Two files to drop in your repo\n\nClaude Code auto-loads `CLAUDE.md` from the project root on every session — that's where persistent context goes. `HANDOFF.md` is the phased work plan it'll follow.\n\n**Step 0 before anything else:** Claude Code cannot see this conversation. Paste the artifact into `src/App.jsx` yourself first. It's one copy-paste and it saves you an hour of regeneration that would produce something worse. The handoff below assumes you've done that, with a fallback path if you haven't.\n\n---\n\n## `CLAUDE.md`\n\n````markdown\n# Gemach Connect\n\nA directory and coordination app for **Gemachs** — Jewish free-loan chesed\norganizations — across North America. Users browse gemachs, bookmark them,\noffer donations, and message organizers to arrange pickup or drop-off.\n\n## Current state\n\n`src/App.jsx` is a working ~1,800-line single-file React app. It is\nfeature-complete but uses a **simulated backend**: a `const api = {...}`\nobject with artificial `setTimeout` latency, backed by `localStorage`.\nEvery visitor gets a private copy of the seed data, so real users cannot\nactually message each other.\n\nThe goal is to modularize it and replace the simulated layer with a real\nExpress + SQLite backend, without regressing any UX behavior.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Vite + React 18, plain JSX (**no TypeScript**)\n- Tailwind CSS v3\n- `lucide-react` for all icons\n- Backend (to be built): Express, `better-sqlite3`, `bcryptjs`,\n  `express-session` + `connect-sqlite3`\n\n## Domain vocabulary\n\n- **Gemach** — a free-loan organization. Has an owner, category, address,\n  weekly hours, and a list of items it currently needs.\n- **Offer** — a donation a user proposes to a gemach.\n  Status: `pending → accepted → completed`, or `declined`.\n- **Thread** — a 1:1 conversation between a gemach owner and one other user,\n  scoped to a specific gemach. Unique on `(gemach_id, user_id)`.\n\n## Data model\n\n```\nUser      { id, name, email, password, phone, city, state, bio, color, joined }\nGemach    { id, ownerId, name, category, description, address, city, state,\n            zip, country, phone, email, website, hours[], needs[],\n            pickupNotes, dropoff, delivery, apptOnly, verified,\n            familiesHelped, createdAt }\nHours[]   { day: 0-6, open: \"HH:MM\", close: \"HH:MM\", closed: bool }\nOffer     { id, gemachId, userId, items, qty, method: \"dropoff\"|\"pickup\",\n            preferredDate, note, status, createdAt }\nThread    { id, gemachId, ownerId, userId, messages[], lastRead: {userId: iso} }\nMessage   { id, senderId, body, at }\nFavorite  { userId, gemachId }\n```\n\nServer tables are `snake_case`; the client contract is `camelCase`. Row\nmapper functions (`toUser`, `toGemach`, `toOffer`, `toMessage`) own that\ntranslation — never leak `snake_case` or SQLite integer booleans to the client.\n\n## Categories\n\n`baby` 🍼 Baby & Kids · `medical` 🩺 Medical Equipment · `simcha` 👰 Simcha & Gowns ·\n`clothing` 👕 Clothing · `food` 🍲 Food & Meals · `furniture` 🛋️ Furniture ·\n`seforim` 📚 Seforim & Books · `party` 🎉 Party & Events · `household` 🏠 Household ·\n`loan` 💵 Free Loan Fund · `tools` 🔧 Tools & Equipment · `bikur` 💙 Bikur Cholim\n\nEach carries a Tailwind gradient (`from-x to-y`) for card headers and a chip\nclass for badges. Defined in `CATEGORIES` with a `catOf(id)` lookup.\n\n## Pages\n\n| Route | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| auth | Split-screen login/signup, demo account button |\n| dashboard | Greeting hero, 4 stat cards, pending requests, nearby gemachs |\n| discover | Search + category chips + state filter + sort, card grid |\n| gemach | Detail: hero, about, needs, pickup notes, hours, contact, organizer |\n| my | Owner's listings with view/edit/delete |\n| form | Create/edit — sectioned form with a 7-day hours editor |\n| requests | Incoming / My offers tabs, status filter, status transitions |\n| messages | Two-pane inbox: thread list + chat panel |\n| saved | Bookmarked gemachs |\n| settings | Profile edit, reset demo data, sign out |\n\n## Non-negotiable UX behaviors\n\nThese are the reason the app feels good. Preserve every one of them.\n\n- **Skeletons, not spinners.** Every page load shows placeholder shapes that\n  match the final layout (`Sk`, `CardSkeleton`).\n- **Bespoke empty states.** Every list has its own icon, headline,\n  explanatory body, and CTA. No generic \"No results.\"\n- **Optimistic updates with rollback.** Favorites toggle instantly. Offer\n  status changes apply before the request resolves. Sent messages appear\n  immediately in a `Sending…` state. All revert on error, with a toast.\n- **Toasts** bottom-right, auto-dismiss at 3.8s, three tones.\n- **Responsive** — 1 column mobile, 2 tablet, 3 desktop. Sidebar collapses\n  to a drawer under `lg`.\n- **\"Open now\"** computed live from `hours[]` against the current time.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Functional components, hooks only. No class components.\n- Tailwind utility classes inline. No CSS modules, no styled-components.\n- Shared primitives live in `src/components/ui/`, one file per component,\n  named exports, re-exported from an `index.js` barrel.\n- Server routes use a `wrap(fn)` error helper and throw `HttpError(status, msg)`.\n- Ownership is checked on **every** mutation, server-side. Never trust the client.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev      # vite + api concurrently\nnpm run build    # production bundle\nnpm start        # NODE_ENV=production, express serves dist/\n```\n\n## Rules for this codebase\n\n- **Do not** invent new dependencies without asking. The list above is it.\n- **Do not** convert to TypeScript.\n- **Do not** restyle or \"improve\" the UI during refactor phases. Structural\n  moves only — the rendered output must be pixel-identical.\n- **Do not** proceed to the next phase in `HANDOFF.md` until the current\n  phase's acceptance criteria pass and the work is committed.\n- Run `npm run build` before declaring any phase complete.\n````\n\n---\n\n## `HANDOFF.md`\n\n````markdown\n# Build Plan\n\nWork through these phases **in order**. Each has acceptance criteria and ends\nin a commit. Stop after each phase and report status before continuing.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 0 — Baseline\n\n**If `src/App.jsx` already contains the full app** (~1,800 lines, exports a\n`App` component wrapping `Root` in `ToastHost`): verify it runs, then skip to\nPhase 1.\n\n**If it doesn't**, scaffold and build it from the spec in `CLAUDE.md`, one\npage at a time, in this order: constants/utils → seed → simulated api →\nUI primitives → Shell → AuthScreen → Dashboard → Discover → GemachCard →\nGemachDetail → GemachForm → MyGemachs → Requests → Messages → Saved →\nSettings → App wiring. Do not attempt it in a single pass.\n\n**Acceptance:** `npm run dev` serves the app. Logging in with\n`sarah@demo.com` / `demo1234` reaches a populated dashboard.\n\n**Commit:** `chore: baseline`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Modularize\n\nPure mechanical extraction. **No behavior changes, no renames, no\n\"improvements.\"** The rendered app must be identical when you're done.\n\nTarget structure:\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── constants.js   CATEGORIES, REGIONS, DAYS, DAYS_SHORT,\n│   │                  AVATAR_COLORS, STATUS, catOf()\n│   ├── utils.js       uid, clone, toMin, fmtTime, isOpenNow,\n│   │                  relTime, fmtDate, initials\n│   ├── seed.js        seed() and its helpers\n│   └── api.js         DB persistence + the api object (still simulated)\n├── components/\n│   ├── ui/\n│   │   ├── Btn.jsx  Field.jsx  Inputs.jsx  Toggle.jsx  Avatar.jsx\n│   │   ├── Badge.jsx  Modal.jsx  EmptyState.jsx  Skeleton.jsx\n│   │   ├── PageHeader.jsx  Toast.jsx\n│   │   └── index.js   barrel re-export\n│   ├── GemachCard.jsx\n│   ├── OfferModal.jsx\n│   ├── QuickMessageModal.jsx\n│   └── Shell.jsx\n├── pages/\n│   ├── AuthScreen.jsx  DashboardPage.jsx  DiscoverPage.jsx\n│   ├── GemachDetail.jsx  GemachFormPage.jsx  MyGemachsPage.jsx\n│   ├── RequestsPage.jsx  MessagesPage.jsx  SavedPage.jsx\n│   └── SettingsPage.jsx\n└── App.jsx            under 100 lines: Root, routing, providers\n```\n\nDo this in three commits — `lib/`, then `components/ui/`, then\n`pages/` + `App.jsx` — verifying the app between each.\n\n**Acceptance:** app is visually and functionally identical. `npm run build`\nclean. `App.jsx` under 100 lines.\n\n**Commits:** `refactor: extract lib`, `refactor: extract ui primitives`,\n`refactor: extract pages`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — Real routing\n\nAdd `react-router-dom` v6. Replace the `nav(name, params)` /\n`route = { name, params }` pattern with URL routes:\n\n```\n/login\n/                       dashboard\n/discover\n/gemach/new\n/gemach/:id\n/gemach/:id/edit\n/requests\n/messages\n/messages/:threadId\n/saved\n/settings\n```\n\n- `Shell` becomes a layout route rendering `<Outlet />`.\n- Unauthenticated users hit `/login`; everything else redirects there.\n- After login, return the user to wherever they were headed.\n- Replace `nav(...)` calls with `useNavigate()` / `<Link>`.\n- Deep links must work on refresh.\n\n**Acceptance:** every page reachable by URL. Browser back/forward behave.\nRefreshing `/gemach/g_3` loads that gemach directly.\n\n**Commit:** `feat: url routing`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — Real backend\n\nBuild Express + SQLite in `server/`.\n\n```\nserver/\n├── db.js              schema, migrations, id(), now(), row mappers\n├── auth.js            hash/verify, requireAuth, wrap, HttpError\n├── seed.js            runSeed() — port src/lib/seed.js to SQL\n├── routes/\n│   ├── auth.js  gemachs.js  offers.js  threads.js  favorites.js  stats.js\n└── index.js           session middleware, route mounts, error handler\n```\n\n### Schema notes\n\n- `hours` and `needs` are JSON `TEXT` columns.\n- Booleans are `INTEGER` 0/1 — mappers convert with `!!`.\n- `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` and `journal_mode = WAL`.\n- `ON DELETE CASCADE` everywhere, so deleting a gemach clears its offers,\n  threads, messages, and favorites automatically.\n- `UNIQUE(gemach_id, user_id)` on `threads`.\n- `thread_reads(thread_id, user_id, at)` composite PK drives unread counts.\n- Indexes on `gemachs(owner_id, category, state)`, `offers(gemach_id, user_id)`,\n  `messages(thread_id, at)`.\n\n### Endpoints\n\n```\nPOST   /api/auth/signup | /login | /logout      GET /api/auth/me\nGET    /api/gemachs?q=&category=&state=&sort=&ownerId=\nGET    /api/gemachs/:id\nPOST   /api/gemachs     PATCH /api/gemachs/:id    DELETE /api/gemachs/:id\nGET    /api/offers?mine=1&incoming=1\nPOST   /api/offers      PATCH /api/offers/:id     DELETE /api/offers/:id\nGET    /api/threads     GET /api/threads/:id\nPOST   /api/threads/find-or-create\nPOST   /api/threads/:id/messages\nGET    /api/favorites   POST /api/favorites/:gemachId/toggle\nGET    /api/stats\n```\n\nResponse shapes must match what the current `api` object returns, field for\nfield, so Phase 4 is a drop-in swap. Specifically:\n\n- Gemachs come back hydrated with `owner`.\n- Offers come back hydrated with `gemach` and `donor`.\n- Thread list items carry `other`, `gemach`, `last`, and `unread`.\n- `/api/stats` returns `{ myGemachs, pendingIncoming, myOffers, unread,\n  saved, totalGemachs, totalFamilies, cities }` where `cities` is the\n  distinct count of `city + state` pairs.\n\n### Authorization rules\n\n| Action | Who |\n|---|---|\n| Edit / delete a gemach | Owner only |\n| Change offer status | Gemach owner only |\n| Edit offer details | Donor, and only while `pending` |\n| Withdraw an offer | Donor, and not once `completed` |\n| Read / post to a thread | The two participants only |\n\nValidate server-side: name required, description ≥ 20 chars, city required,\nemail required, category must exist, `method` in `('dropoff','pickup')`,\n`status` in the four allowed values. Reject unknown fields —\n`verified`, `familiesHelped`, `ownerId`, and `createdAt` are server-controlled.\n\n### Seed\n\n`runSeed()` inserts the full dataset inside a single `db.transaction()`:\n**8 users, 16 gemachs, 7 offers in mixed statuses, 5 conversations.** Keep\nthe original copy verbatim — the realistic descriptions and message threads\nare what make the demo land. Hash every password with bcrypt. Seed only when\n`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users` is 0.\n\n### Wiring\n\n- Vite proxy `/api` → `http://localhost:3001`\n- `\"dev\": \"concurrently -n web,api -c cyan,magenta \\\"vite\\\" \\\"node --watch server/index.js\\\"\"`\n- Sessions in `connect-sqlite3`, cookie `httpOnly`, `sameSite: 'lax'`,\n  `secure` only in production.\n- In production, Express serves `dist/` with an SPA catch-all.\n- SQLite files land in `data/` — add `data/` to `.gitignore`.\n\n**Acceptance:** `curl` each endpoint successfully. Signup rejects duplicate\nemails with 409. A non-owner gets 403 patching someone else's gemach.\nDeleting a gemach cascades.\n\n**Commits:** one per route file.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4 — Swap the client API\n\nRewrite `src/lib/api.js` as thin `fetch` wrappers. Keep the exact same method\nnames and signatures so pages don't change.\n\n```js\nconst request = async (path, { method = 'GET', body } = {}) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api${path}`, {\n    method,\n    credentials: 'include',\n    headers: body ? { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } : undefined,\n    body: body ? JSON.stringify(body) : undefined,\n  });\n  if (res.status === 204) return null;\n  const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.error || 'Request failed.');\n  return data;\n};\n```\n\nDelete: all `setTimeout` latency, the `AUTO_REPLIES` simulation, every\n`localStorage` call, `ensureDB`, `persist`, `loadDB`, `resetDB`, and the\nin-memory `DB` object.\n\n**Acceptance:** app works end to end against the server. Nothing in\n`src/lib/api.js` references `localStorage`.\n\n**Commit:** `feat: real api client`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5 — Frontend reconciliation\n\nThe UI reaches into the fake DB in a few places. These will crash or fail\nsilently otherwise:\n\n| Where | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Root` | `api.favoriteIds()` is **synchronous** | Now async — `await api.listFavorites()` and map to ids. Two call sites: the mount effect and `onAuthed`. |\n| `Root` | `refreshBadges` guards on `DB?.session?.userId` | Guard on `user` instead |\n| `Root` | `ensureDB()` on mount | Delete |\n| `SettingsPage` | `resetDB()` + `window.location.reload()` | Either remove the feature or add `POST /api/admin/reset` gated behind `ALLOW_RESET=1` |\n| `MessagesPage` | 3s poll | Keep — it works against the real API |\n| Messages generally | Auto-replies are gone | Threads stay quiet until a real second user replies. Test with `rivky@example.com` / `demo1234` in a private window. |\n\nAlso: surface 401s globally. If any request fails with 401, clear the user\nand route to `/login`.\n\n**Acceptance:** no console errors. Favorites, badges, and messaging all work.\nTwo browser profiles can hold a real conversation.\n\n**Commit:** `fix: reconcile client with real api`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6 — Harden\n\n1. Add Vitest + Supertest. Cover the authorization matrix above — the 403\n   cases matter more than the happy paths.\n2. Rate-limit `/api/auth/*` (`express-rate-limit`, 10/15min per IP).\n3. `.env.example` with `SESSION_SECRET`, `PORT`, `NODE_ENV`.\n4. `README.md`: what a gemach is, setup, demo credentials, deploy notes.\n5. Deployment: **SQLite does not survive on Vercel** — serverless\n   filesystems are ephemeral. Target Fly.io, Railway, or Render with a\n   persistent volume. If Vercel is required, swap `better-sqlite3` for\n   `@neondatabase/serverless` against Neon Postgres; the schema ports nearly\n   1:1 (`TEXT`→`text`, `INTEGER` bools→`boolean`, JSON columns→`jsonb`).\n\n**Commit:** `chore: tests, docs, deploy config`\n````\n\n---\n\n## Kickoff prompt\n\n```bash\ncd gemach-connect\nclaude\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```\nRead CLAUDE.md and HANDOFF.md.\n\nStart with Phase 0: confirm src/App.jsx contains the full working app and\nthat `npm run dev` serves it. Report what you find before touching anything.\n\nWork one phase at a time. After each phase, run `npm run build`, verify the\nacceptance criteria, commit, and stop for my review. Don't start the next\nphase until I say go.\n\nFor Phase 1 specifically: this is a mechanical extraction. Do not rename\nanything, do not refactor logic, do not adjust styling. The app must render\nidentically.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Claude Code workflow notes\n\n**Use plan mode for the big phases.** `Shift+Tab` toggles it. Phase 3 especially — let it lay out the schema and route structure before it writes anything, so you catch design problems early rather than after six files land.\n\n**Permissions.** It'll ask before each file write and shell command. For the mechanical phases that gets tedious; `/permissions` lets you allowlist `Edit`, `Bash(npm run build)`, and `Bash(git commit:*)`. Keep `Bash(rm:*)` on manual approval.\n\n**Context hygiene.** `/clear` between phases. Each phase is independent, and carrying Phase 1's file contents into Phase 3 just crowds the window. `/compact` if you're mid-phase and running long.\n\n**Checkpointing.** Commit at every green state yourself if it doesn't. `Esc Esc` rewinds the conversation; `git reset --hard` rewinds the code. You want both available.\n\n**When it drifts.** The most common failure on Phase 1 is \"helpfully\" improving code during extraction. If you see a diff that touches logic, reject it and re-state: *structural moves only, rendered output must be identical.*\n\n**Watch specifically for** — in Phase 4, it will probably miss the synchronous `favoriteIds()` call. That's why it's called out explicitly in Phase 5's table. If it claims Phase 4 is done, check `Root` before believing it.",
